#NEXUS

[ poust2020a_fig10: Dromaeosaurid time tree. Internal labels from the three nested boxes (Paraves, Dromaeosauridae, Microraptorinae). Mahakala sits inside the Dromaeosauridae box and is encoded inside the clade, as drawn. Polytomies: the six eudromaeosaurs on one vertical with a four-taxon clade, the four achillobator-group taxa, and four microraptorines with (Sinornithosaurus, Wulong). 21 tips, 3 polytomies (7, 4, 5 children); 3 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Random-sample case (seed 20261114). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

